      "hostOrNarrator": null,
      "focusOrTheme": "Plea bargaining system, innocent defendants pleading guilty, prosecutorial pressure, inadequate defense counsel, impact of poverty on justice outcomes.",
      "summaryNotes": "The episode examines the plea bargaining system through cases in Hearne, Texas, focusing on Erma Faye Stewart and Regina Kelly, who were wrongly implicated in a drug sweep. It highlights the pressures of the plea system, inadequate counsel, and unreliable informants.",
